{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#director-of-career-success-and-community-engagement": {
      "title": "Director of Career Success and Community Engagement",
      "description": "Director of Career Success and Community Engagement. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Director of Career Success and Community Engagement . The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Director of Career Success and Community Engagement provides visionary leadership for developing strategic employer partnerships, experiential learning opportunities, and comprehensive career readiness initiatives that prepare University of Dubuque students for meaningful careers and lives of purpose. The Director serves as the University's primary liaison to regional, state, and national employers while leading a campus-wide career success ecosystem that integrates academic affairs, student life, athletics, residence life, alumni relations, and community engagement. This position develops innovative community partnerships that expand internships, apprenticeships, mentorships, experiential learning, sponsorships, and employment opportunities; while strengthening the University's workforce development mission. The Director works collaboratively across campus to assist students in graduating with professional experience, career competencies, meaningful employer relationships, and a post-graduation plan aligned with the University's mission of educating and forming the whole person. Primary Responsibilities: Facilitate the development and implementation of a comprehensive University-wide Career Success Strategic Plan Develop annual departmental goals, assessment plans, and strategic performance metrics Supervise professional staff, graduate assistants, interns, and student employees Serve as the University's primary relationship manager with regional, national, and global employers Develop strategic partnerships that provide internships, cooperative education experiences, clinical placements, apprenticeships, corporate mentoring, employer-sponsored projects, recruitment pipelines, and collaborative international experiences Coordinate annual career fairs, networking events, employer panels, and professional development workshops Collaborate with campus partners to embed career readiness throughout the student experience Support faculty in integrating career preparation into academic curricula Coordinate employer site visits and industry immersion experiences Assist in developing Employer-in-Residence and Executive-in-Residence programs Develop strategic partnerships with the Greater Dubuque Development Corporation, local chambers of commerce, healthcare systems, manufacturing partners, financial institutions, and nonprofit organizations Collaborate with regional employers to identify workforce needs and emerging employment trends Coordinate workforce pipeline initiatives with community and economic development organizations Collaborate with campus partners to collect, analyze, and report data regarding internship participation, career readiness, completion, graduate placement, graduate school enrollment, employer satisfaction, student engagement, career outcomes, and First Destination Survey results Serve as campus administrator for: Handshake, career management platforms, employer relationship management systems, and career assessment software Represent the University at professional organizations, employer meetings, workforce initiatives, and higher education conferences Serve as a Title IX Campus Security Authority Support the University's Christian mission and institutional values Willingness and ability to be an active participant in following applicable safety rules and regulations, including necessary training and drills Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Exceptional relationship-building and partnership development skills Proven business development and external relations experience Strategic planning and organizational leadership abilities Knowledge of workforce development and labor market trends Experience developing employer partnerships and experiential learning opportunities Strong presentation, communication, and public speaking skills Budget development and fiscal management experience Assessment, data analytics, and program evaluation expertise Ability to collaborative across multiple campus divisions Ability to inspire innovation and entrepreneurial thinking Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills Requirements: Graduate degree required in Higher Education Administration, Business Administration, Student Affairs, Human Resources, Organizational Leadership, Counseling, or a related field Five or more years of progressively responsible leadership experience in career services, employer relations, workforce development, corporate partnerships, university advancement, talent acquisition, or related areas Success in developing strategic partnerships with employers and community organizations Experience supervising professional staff and managing budgets To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Director of Career Success and Community Engagement position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#childcare-lead-teacher": {
      "title": "Childcare Lead Teacher",
      "description": "Childcare Lead Teacher. Love working with little ones and helping them grow, learn, and thrive? Join the University of Dubuque! We are a faith-based University seeking a caring and enthusiastic, full-time Childcare Lead Teacher to join our childcare team. Benefits: Four weeks of vacation with one week available after 90 days of employment Tuition benefits for the employee after one year of employment Tuition benefits for eligible dependents beginning immediately Retirement match- dollar for dollar up to 5% with eligible match up to 7% Medical, dental, and vision insurance Life insurance and long-term disability Childcare center on campus with discounted rates Position Summary: The Lead Childcare Teacher plays a vital role in creating a nurturing and stimulating learning environment for young children. This position is responsible for planning and implementing developmentally appropriate daily activities aligned with the Creative Curriculum, utilizing diverse teaching techniques to foster children's cognitive, social, emotional, and physical growth. Additionally, this role involves guiding and mentoring assistant teachers and other staff, promoting their professional development, and actively fostering a welcoming, inclusive atmosphere that celebrates diversity and positive social interactions. Primary Responsibilities: Plan daily activities and post weekly lesson plans based on Creative Curriculum, along with utilizing a variety of teaching techniques (storytelling, multi-sensory, games, etc.) to teach children and help them explore their interests Maintain a clean and organized classroom, ensuring the safety of children during all activities and responding appropriately to emergencies Help facilitate daily activities that are developmentally appropriate for the age group, promoting cognitive, social, emotional, and physical development Communicate effectively with parents regarding their child's progress, addressing concerns, and building strong relationships Provide guidance to assistant teachers and other staff members, and helping them develop their skills Promote diversity, positive social interactions and a welcoming atmosphere for all children Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Effective communication with children, parents, and coworkers Ability to work with young children and understand their needs Ability to multitask and prioritize multiple responsibilities Ability to work collaboratively with other staff members, including assistants, building strong teamwork, along with a cohesive and supportive learning environment Ability to bend, lift up to 50 lbs., stoop, kneel, and be on your feet for extended periods of time Work with children from diverse backgrounds and cultures Requirements: High school diploma Required; Associate degree Preferred Current certification in First Aid, CPR, Universal Precautions, and Mandatory Reporting training is preferred: ability to obtain certifications after employment is required Previous experience working with children is required Ability to work a flexible schedule is preferred Excellent communication skills - verbal, written, and interpersonal To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Childcare Lead Teacher position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#aviation-maintenance-technician": {
      "title": "Aviation Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Aviation Maintenance Technician. The Aviation Department at the University of Dubuque is seeking an Aviation Maintenance Technician . The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Hours: Monday - Friday, first shift with anticipation to move towards Tuesday - Saturday Position Summary: An experienced Aircraft Mechanic holding a valid Airframe and Powerplant (A&P) license, responsible for the inspection, maintenance, and repair of general aviation aircraft, specifically Cessna Skyhawks and Piper Seminoles. Ensures all work is performed in accordance with FAA regulations, manufacturer specifications, and UD standards. Duties include routine scheduled maintenance, troubleshooting mechanical issues, performing engine and airframe repairs, and completing necessary documentation. Works closely with other maintenance personnel to ensure aircraft safety, airworthiness, and readiness for flight operations. Primary Responsibilities: Support and assist in the maintenance of UD aircraft and related equipment Provide administrative and maintenance support to the Director of Maintenance Ensure maintenance of all UD aircraft in accordance with applicable FAA, OSHA, and UD policies Assist in reconciliation of aircraft maintenance logs and other maintenance aircraft related documents Assist with resolving discrepancies or other maintenance related issues by coordinating with flight center staff Assist in training and onboarding of incoming work-study staff Perform other duties in support of the aviation department and the University's M ission Skills and Abilities: Prior fixed-wing or rotor-wing aircraft maintenance experience preferred Prior mechanical maintenance experience Ability to bend, stoop, and kneel Must be able to lift at least 40lbs Must be able to stand on your feet for long periods of time Effective communication skills; both orally and writing Exceptional skills using Microsoft Office Ability to relate to a culturally diverse university community and interact effectively with other as well as work collaboratively with other departments Qualifications: Minimum of high school diploma or equivalent; Associates Degree Preferred A&P certificate required Valid US driver's license Flexibility with schedule when the need arises (potential on-call, nights, and weekends) Willingness to work overtime if needed To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Aviation Maintenance Technician position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#evening-supervisor-charles-c-myers-library": {
      "title": "Evening Supervisor - Charles C. Myers Library",
      "description": "Evening Supervisor - Charles C. Myers Library. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking an Evening Supervisor for the Charles C. Myers Library. Position Summary: The Evening Supervisor helps create and sustain the Charles C. Myers Library as a welcoming learning studio and idea lab during evening hours by providing research and information assistance, supervising student employees, supporting the use of library resources and technologies, and fostering an environment of curiosity, collaboration, and academic engagement. This position plays a key role in connecting students with the resources, spaces, and support needed for learning, research, and project development while ensuring smooth library operations and high-quality public service. Regular hours are Monday through Thursday evenings when classes are in session, with additional hours during academic breaks and summer sessions determined in consultation with the Assistant Director for Public Services. Primary Responsibilities: Provide research, information, and resource assistance to students, faculty, and staff during evening hours Assist with supervising, training, and supporting student workers, ensuring a high standard of service and engagement with library users Assist with circulation services, equipment lending, reserves, and user account inquiries Support students in the effective use of library resources, learning technologies, and collaborative workspaces Troubleshoot basic technology issues related to library equipment, digital resources, and user access Foster a welcoming, inclusive, and productive environment that encourages learning, exploration, collaboration, and responsible scholarship Monitor library spaces to ensure safe, effective, and appropriate use of facilities and resources Communicate effectively with library staff regarding operational issues, user needs, and service improvements to maintain continuity across shifts Perform opening and/or closing procedures as assigned Support library programs, services, and initiatives that advance student learning, creativity, and engagement Support library operations during academic breaks and summer sessions, as scheduled Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Strong interpersonal, customer service, and communication skills with the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty, staff, and visitors Commitment to creating a welcoming environment that supports learning, collaboration, and student success Ability to supervise, mentor, and provide directions to student employees Ability to support users in locating, evaluating, and utilizing information resources and learning technologies Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot basic technology issues Ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and manage responsibilities during evening hours Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to balance multiple priorities Adaptability, initiative, and willingness to contribute to evolving library services, programs, and spaces Qualifications: Undergraduate Degree Required; Graduate Degree Preferred Experience providing customer service, educational support, student services, or other public-facing work Demonstrate proficiency with computers, office software, online research tools, and common digital technologies Available to work scheduled evening hours during the academic year Experience supervising, mentoring, or leading student employees or other staff preferred Experience working in a library, learning commons, academic support center, educational setting, or customer-service environment preferred To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Evening Supervisor for the Charles C. Myers Library position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#security-officer": {
      "title": "Security Officer",
      "description": "Security Officer. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Security Officer (Full-time, 3 rd shift). The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Security Guard is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment for all students, faculty, staff, and visitors on campus. This role involves regular foot patrols of university grounds and buildings, enforcing university policies, responding to emergencies, and documenting incidents with accuracy and attention to detail. Security Guards are also tasked with opening and closing campus facilities, issuing parking violations, and operating a multi-line phone and radio dispatch system to coordinate responses effectively. Security Guards play a critical role in supporting the Mission of the university by ensuring a secure and welcoming campus environment. Primary Responsibilities: Open and close campus facilities Issue parking violations Maintain security and safety of people and property on campus by patrolling on foot Enforce policies in support of the University's mission Answer emergency and non-emergency calls and document important information Respond to any issues and follow-up by coordinating with the appropriate departments or officers Operate and manage a multi-line telephone system Use the radio, phone, or computer to direct officers to the appropriate sites Prioritize and organize calls according to urgency Maintain and update call logs, call records and other important documentation Update requests for access from various departments through the controlled access program Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Familiar with reporting requirements of the Clery Act for Higher Education Must be detail orientated and accurate Ability to walk and climb stairs Knowledge of basic security and fire inspection procedures Quick decision-making skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills Ability to multi-task and work under pressure May be required to walk or stand for extended periods of time May be required to work outdoors in inclement weather May be required to lift, push or pull up to 50 lbs. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Valid driver's license Basic computer knowledge Ability to read and comprehend basic written and verbal instructions This position will require night and weekend work. (2nd shift $0.50 shift differential and 3rd shift $0.65 shift differential) To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Security Officer position, please submit a cover letter, resume, three professional references, and UD employment application, located on our website http://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/, to HR@dbq.edu or to the Director of Human Resources, at the University of Dubuque, 2000 University Avenue, Dubuque, IA 52001. Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#custodians": {
      "title": "Custodians",
      "description": "Custodians. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking Custodians . The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The University of Dubuque is seeking a dependable and detail-oriented Custodian to help maintain a clean, safe, and welcoming environment across campus facilities. This position plays a vital role in supporting the daily operations of the University by ensuring classrooms, offices, restrooms, and common areas are cleaned and maintained to high standards. Successful candidates will be self-motivated, able to work both independently and as part of a team and committed to supporting the mission of the University. Primary Responsibilities: Maintain cleanliness of campus buildings, including classrooms, offices, restrooms, and common areas Vacuum, sweep, and mop floors to ensure a safe and sanitary environment Deep clean bathrooms- showers, stools, tile, etc. Wash walls and windows Empty trash and recycling bins and ensure proper disposal Assist with setup and teardown for campus events, including moving furniture, equipment, and supplies Operate floor and carpet machines Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Ability to follow checklists and complete assigned tasks without close supervision Works well independently and as part of a team Dependable, punctual, and committed to maintaining a clean, safe environment Ability to bend, stoop, and kneel Ability to climb a 6' ladder Must be able to lift at least 40 lbs. Must be able to stand on your feet for long periods of time Qualifications: Minimum of high school diploma or equivalent Driver's license preferred Current Openings (subject to change): Friday - Monday 5:00 am - 3:30 pm Monday - Friday 3:00 pm - 11:30 pm Monday - Friday 5:00 am - 1:30 pm Saturday - Tuesday 1:00 pm - 11:30 pm Includes a $0.50 per hour shift differential for 2nd shift To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Custodian position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#facilities-maintenance-worker-specializing-in-hvac": {
      "title": "Facilities Maintenance Worker specializing in HVAC",
      "description": "Facilities Maintenance Worker specializing in HVAC. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Facilities Maintenance Worker specializing in HVAC . The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Facilities Maintenance Worker will be responsible for performing general maintenance and repair duties across campus buildings and facilities, with a specialization in HVAC systems. The ideal candidate will be a dependable, self-motivated individual who takes pride in their work and values teamwork in a mission-driven environment. Primary Responsibilities: Perform skilled HVAC work, including installation, preventative maintenance, and troubleshooting on equipment such as heat pumps, rooftop units, boilers, furnaces, central heating systems, and various refrigeration equipment Perform skilled and semi-skilled carpentry, remodels, & new construction Perform preventative maintenance on equipment & buildings Complete all required paperwork in a timely manner Perform routine maintenance tasks including plumbing, electrical, HVAC, carpentry and painting Perform snow removal related activities when necessary Assist with event setup and campus preparation Conduct inspections to identify and resolve issues proactively Maintain a clean and safe work environment in accordance with safety regulations Repair and/or replace concrete, plaster walls, paint walls, ceilings, fixtures, etc. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Ability to work in a variety of weather conditions Occasional heavy lifting up to 100 lbs. is required Ability to stand on your feet for long periods of time, bend, stoop, and kneel Ability to climb a 12' ladder, work on scaffolding & operate an aerial lift Excellent communication skills - verbal, written, and interpersonal Qualifications: Minimum of high school diploma or equivalent Journeyperson HVAC License preferred or Completion of associate's degree from a 2-year college or technical school with a certificate in HVAC-R Experience with DDC (Direct Digital Control) systems; familiarity with Johnson Controls, Trane, and Schneider Electric systems Strong knowledge of electronic/digital controls systems, low voltage electrical systems, HVAC control systems Must have a valid driver's license Respond to calls for emergency services including snow removal on nights and weekends Ability to pass a background check Current Opening (subject to change): Monday - Friday 7:15 am - 3:45 pm Compensation will be determined based on factors including market conditions, organizational considerations, and the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate. Includes a $0.50 per hour shift differential for 2nd shift To apply with a growing faith based University for the Facilities Maintenance Worker specializing in HVAC position, please submit a cover letter, resume, three professional references, and UD employment application, located on our website, to HR@dbq.edu or to the Director of Human Resources, at the University of Dubuque, 2000 University Avenue, Dubuque, IA 52001. Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#facilities-maintenance-worker-specializing-in-plumbing": {
