    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#facilities-maintenance-worker-specializing-in-electrical": {
      "title": "Facilities Maintenance Worker specializing in Electrical",
      "description": "Facilities Maintenance Worker specializing in Electrical. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Facilities Maintenance Worker specializing in Electrical . The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match Position Summary: The Facilities Maintenance Worker will be responsible for performing general maintenance and repair duties across campus buildings and facilities, with a specialization in electrical systems. The ideal candidate will be a dependable, self-motivated individual who takes pride in their work and values teamwork in a mission-driven environment. Primary Responsibilities: Perform skilled journeyman-level electrical work and demonstrate proficiency in the trade Maintain, repair, install, and modify electrical systems, fire panels, food service equipment, and fixtures Assist in troubleshooting HVAC and refrigeration equipment, including heat pumps, rooftop units, boilers, furnaces, central heating systems, and various refrigeration units Perform skilled and semi-skilled carpentry, remodels, & new construction Perform preventative maintenance on equipment & buildings Complete all required paperwork in a timely manner Perform routine maintenance tasks including plumbing, electrical, HVAC, carpentry and painting Perform snow removal related activities when necessary Assist with event setup and campus preparation Conduct inspections to identify and resolve issues proactively Maintain a clean and safe work environment in accordance with safety regulations Repair and/or replace concrete, plaster walls, paint walls, ceilings, fixtures, etc. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Ability to work in a variety of weather conditions Occasional heavy lifting up to 100 lbs. is required Ability to stand on your feet for long periods of time, bend, stoop, and kneel Ability to climb a 12' ladder, work on scaffolding & operate an aerial lift Excellent communication skills - verbal, written, and interpersonal Qualifications: Minimum of high school diploma or equivalent Experience in electrical construction, maintenance, repair, and Fire Alarm Panel systems Journeyperson Electrical License preferred Must have a valid driver's license Respond to calls for emergency services including snow removal on nights and weekends Ability to pass a background check Current Opening (subject to change): Monday - Friday 7:15 am - 3:45 pm Compensation will be determined based on factors including market conditions, organizational considerations, and the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate. Includes a $0.50 per hour shift differential for 2nd shift To apply with a growing faith based University for the Facilities Maintenance Worker specializing in Electrical position, please submit a cover letter, resume, three professional references, and UD employment application, located on our website, to HR@dbq.edu or to the Director of Human Resources, at the University of Dubuque, 2000 University Avenue, Dubuque, IA 52001. Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#facilities-maintenance-worker": {
      "title": "Facilities Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "Facilities Maintenance Worker. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith based University that is seeking a Facilities Maintenance Worker . The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Hours: Tuesday - Saturday 3:00 p.m. - 11:30 p.m. Includes a $0.50 per hour shift differential for 2nd shift Primary Responsibilities: Repair and maintain equipment, plumbing, electrical, boiler system, HVAC, locks, and buildings in accordance with building codes Perform skilled and semi-skilled carpentry, remodels, and new construction Perform preventative maintenance on equipment and buildings Complete all required paperwork in a timely manner Perform a variety of basic electrical repairs and installations Perform snow removal related activities when necessary Restore and/or replace various types of furniture, doors, windows, floors, roofs, etc. Repair and/or replace concrete, plaster walls, paint walls, ceilings, fixtures, etc. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission including overtime assignments and emergency call-in work Requirements: Must have a valid driver's license Minimum of high school diploma or equivalent Completion of electrical, plumbing, and/or HVAC training courses are highly preferred Minimum of 4 years related experience Ability to work in a variety of weather conditions Occasional heavy lifting up to 100 lbs. is required Ability to stand on your feet for long periods of time, bend, stoop, and kneel Excellent communication skills - verbal, written, and interpersonal Ability to climb a 12' ladder, work on scaffolding, and operate an aerial lift To apply with a growing faith based University for the Facilities Maintenance Worker position, please submit a cover letter, resume, three professional references, and UD employment application, located on our website, to HR@dbq.edu or to the Director of Human Resources, at the University of Dubuque, 2000 University Avenue, Dubuque, IA 52001. Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#student-accounts-collection-coordinator": {
      "title": "Student Accounts Collection Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Accounts Collection Coordinator. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Student Accounts Collection Coordinator . The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Student Accounts Collection Coordinator is a member of the Student Accounts team with primary responsibility for managing delinquent receivables. This position ensures the timely generation of account statements and coordinates effective collection efforts while providing exceptional customer service to students, families, faculty, staff, and external partners. Primary Responsibilities: Generate and distribute billing for student accounts and institutional loans Counsel students and families regarding billing statements, payment options, and account discrepancies, and establish payment plans in accordance with university policy Determine and process account write-offs in compliance with university policy and applicable regulations Credit report delinquent accounts to credit bureaus Ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations related to debt collection Review accounts with outstanding balances to determine transcript eligibility Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills Excellent knowledge of Microsoft products (Excel, Word, etc.) Ability to use discretion and confidentiality in accordance with FERPA and University matters Ability to work independently and collaboratively Strong understanding of receivables management and credit bureau reporting Ability to remain seated at a workstation for extended periods of time Strong organizational, time management, and problem-solving abilities Qualifications: Associate Degree Required; Undergraduate Degree Preferred 2-4 years of experience with accounts receivable with specific focus on credit reporting To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Student Accounts Collection Coordinator position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#enterprise-application-data-services-specialist": {
      "title": "Enterprise Application & Data Services Specialist",
      "description": "Enterprise Application & Data Services Specialist. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking an Enterprise Application & Data Services Specialist . The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Enterprise Application and Data Services Specialist will play a key role in helping the University of Dubuque to optimize data quality and workflow processes, assist with system integrations, and improve reporting and analytical support. This role will collaborate closely with and support individuals and departments across campus to strengthen our use of technical systems and improve efficiencies related to technology, data and processes. Primary Responsibilities: Identify, develop and correct procedures for monitoring accuracy and quality of data Work with stakeholders to educate, assist and update data and processes Write and maintain stored procedures and functions to extract, transform and report on data Provide recommendations and technical expertise regarding the use of all University systems and the data within said systems Design, develop and generate reports to meet the needs of users across campus in a timely, efficient and accurate manner Provide data-driven insights by collecting, analyzing and reporting on trends to support strategic decision making Create forms and workflows to assist in improving processes and data flow between and within departments across campus Automate processes to allow faculty and staff to spend more time interacting with students versus performing arduous tasks and unneeded paperwork Be a partner that others across campus can rely upon to provide high-quality assistance and insight regarding needs related to systems, data and processes Understand proper integration and documentation of the use of all software tools used to manage the University of Dubuque's data Keep abreast of upgrades to all systems and how these will help deliver the best data and most efficient process improvement to end users Research and have knowledge of new technologies as well as investigate unused modules of current systems as potential ways to improve processes Document all procedures so they can be understood and supported by other team members as well as end users Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's mission Position Skills and Abilities: Strong technical aptitude Proficient in problem-solving project management and analytical skills Strong understanding of process improvement and workflow development Ability to manage several high-priority projects simultaneously while producing quality work in a timely and accurate manner Excellent communication and collaboration skills Ability to develop, build and strengthen relationships to create partnerships with stakeholders from all areas of the university Strong attention to detail Ability to investigate and understand processes to deliver timely, accurate and actionable solutions Strong problem solving and analytical skills Self-motivated and highly responsible Ability to work alone as well as collaborate with others Requirements: Undergraduate Degree Required; Computer emphasis preferred or related business experience Experience using report writers, preferably SQL Server Reporting Services and Power BI Strong understanding and experience of relational database applications Experience with TSQL in developing SQL scripts, procedures and functions To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Enterprise Application & Data Services Specialist position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#enterprise-systems-integration-analyst-programmer": {
      "title": "Enterprise Systems Integration Analyst/Programmer",
      "description": "Enterprise Systems Integration Analyst/Programmer. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking an Enterprise Systems Integration Analyst/Programmer . The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Enterprise Systems Integration Analyst/Programmer will play a critical role in supporting, enhancing, and integrating the University of Dubuque's enterprise systems. This position focuses on systems analysis, data integration, automation, and technical problem solving to improve data flow, system reliability, and user experience across campus. The role collaborates closely with functional departments to understand business needs and translates them into scalable, maintainable technical solutions that support the University's mission. Primary Responsibilities: Collaborate with stakeholders across campus to understand business processes, data needs and system challenges Analyze existing systems and workflows and recommend technical or process improvements! Translate functional requirements into technical designs and specifications Develop, maintain, and enhance scripts, procedures, and automation to support institutional systems and workflows Utilize scripting and programming languages (e.g., Python, JavaScript, T-SQL) to support data processing, integration and automation Ensure code quality, documentation and adherence to best practices Create forms and workflows to assist in improving processes and data flow between and within departments across campus Automate processes to allow faculty and staff to spend more time interacting with students versus performing arduous tasks and unneeded paperwork Be a partner that others across campus can rely upon to provide high-quality assistance and insight regarding needs related to systems, data and processes Design, implement, and support integrations between systems using APIs, data feeds and other integration methods Monitor and troubleshoot integrations to ensure data accuracy, reliability and performance Collaborate with vendors and internal teams on system upgrades, patches and integration changes Support and enhance web-based applications, forms and campus portal functionality Assist with the configuration and scripting of user-facing systems to improve usability, accessibility, and overall user experience Work collaboratively with stakeholders to identify opportunities to better leverage existing web platforms Support reporting and analytics initiatives by ensuring reliable data availability and integration Assist in the development of reports, dashboards and data extracts used for operational and strategic decision-making Serve as a secondary support resource for key enterprise applications, learning system configurations, scripting, and workflows as needed to ensure continuity of operations Document system logic, integrations, procedures and technical configurations so they can be supported by others Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's mission Position Skills and Abilities: Strong analytical, problem-solving, and technical aptitude Ability to manage multiple priorities while producing accurate, high-quality work Excellent communication and collaboration skills, including the ability to work effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders Ability to investigate and understand business processes to deliver effective technical solutions Strong attention to detail and commitment to documentation and maintainability Self-motivated, adaptable, and highly responsible Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team environment Experience collaborating with functional users to improve processes through technology Requirements: Undergraduate Degree Required; bachelor's degree in computer science, Information Systems, Software Engineering, or a related field preferred, or equivalent professional experience Familiar with workflow automation, forms platforms, or document management solutions Experience working with relational databases and SQL-based systems Experience with scripting or programming languages such as Python and JavaScript Familiar with API-based integrations and data exchange concepts Experience in supporting or developing web-based systems or applications Experience working in a higher education or similarly complex, multi-system environment Experience supporting or integrating enterprise systems such as student information systems, document management systems, learning management systems or campus portals To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Enterprise Systems Integration Analyst/Programmer position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#dispatcher": {
      "title": "Dispatcher",
      "description": "Dispatcher. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Dispatcher in the Safety and Security Department. The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The University Dispatcher plays a vital role in maintaining campus safety by serving as the central communication hub for the Department of Safety and Security. This position is responsible for receiving and coordinating responses to emergency and non-emergency calls, managing radio and telephone communications, and dispatching security personnel to incidents across campus. The Dispatcher also monitors and maintains detailed records, manages access requests through the University's controlled access system, and may occasionally perform foot patrols or fill in for security officers as needed. Primary Responsibilities: Answer emergency and non-emergency calls promptly and professionally, gathering and documenting critical information for appropriate response Respond to any issues and follow-up by coordinating with the appropriate departments or officers Operate and manage a multi-line telephone system Use the radio, phone, or computer to direct officers to the appropriate sites Prioritize and organize calls according to urgency Maintain and update call logs, call records and other important documentation Update requests for access from various departments through the controlled access program Fill-in as a security officer including foot patrol Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Must be detail orientated and accurate Ability to multi-task and work under pressure Quick decision-making skills Prior experience working with phone systems, computers, surveillance cameras, and portable radios Calm and professional demeanor under pressure, especially during emergencies or high-stress situations Ability to remain seated at a workstation for extended periods of time Ability to walk and climb stairs for foot patrol Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Valid driver's license Knowledge of basic security and fire inspection procedures is preferred This is a 1 st shift position from 7am-3pm Tuesday-Saturday. To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Dispatcher position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#admission-counselor": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Admission Counselor. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking an Admission Counselor in the Office of Admission. The University of Dubuque offers an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Admission Counselor is responsible for executing strategic undergraduate recruitment efforts within an assigned geographic territory. This position represents the University of Dubuque at high schools, college fairs, community events, and campus programs, while providing individualized admission counseling to prospective students and families. The Admission Counselor collaborates with admission leadership to develop territory-specific recruitment strategies, evaluate applications, analyze enrollment data, and contribute to achieving institutional enrollment goals. Primary Responsibilities: Manage all recruitment activities within assigned geographic territory to support undergraduate enrollment goals Provide admission counseling to prospective students, parents, and school counselors regarding admission policies, procedures, academic programs, and financial aid opportunities Represent the University of Dubuque at college fairs, high school visits, receptions, and on-campus recruitment events Collaborate with the Associate Dean of Admission to develop and implement a strategic territory recruitment plan and travel schedule Evaluate admission applications and analyze enrollment funnel data to monitor recruitment progress and improve student conversion outcomes Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to effectively present information to diverse audiences Ability to build and maintain positive relationships with students, families, school counselors, and campus partners Strong organizational, planning, and time-management skills with attention to detail Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as a member of a collaborative team Proficiency in utilizing data and enrollment management systems to support recruitment strategies and decision-making Requirements: Undergraduate Degree Required in Business Administration, Marketing, Communications, or a related field; Graduate Degree preferred Previous experience in college admission, recruitment, sales, marketing, or a related field preferred Ability to travel extensively and transport admission materials, displays, and equipment; valid driver's license required Demonstrate ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds and cultures Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends, and perform event-related activities that may require extended standing, walking, and climbing stairs To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Admission Counselor position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#social-media-specialist": {
      "title": "Social Media Specialist",
      "description": "Social Media Specialist. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Social Media Specialist . The University of Dubuque offers a competitive wage and an excellent benefits package including tuition remission, paid holidays, vacation and sick time, and a retirement match. Position Summary: The Social Media Specialist develops and executes engaging social media strategies that enhance the University of Dubuque's visibility and authentically showcase the University to prospective students, current students, alumni, and stakeholders. This position creates and manages multimedia content, collaborates with campus constituents, maintains the social media calendar, monitors analytics and engagement, and supports campaigns across current and emerging platforms. The ideal candidate is a creative, collaborative communicator with strong digital content skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities in support of the University's mission. Primary Responsibilities: Develop and execute a comprehensive and creative social media strategy that enhances UD's visibility and showcases the University to prospective students and stakeholders Reach out and collaborate with key campus constituents to establish and drive user-generated content to authentically amplify UD's online voice Collaborate with the Office of University Relations' team to ensure social media strategies align with other marketing and communication efforts and department initiatives Manage a robust social media calendar of consistent social media features along with campaign initiatives that utilize current as well as emerging social media platforms and tactics to support strategies and initiatives Follow and evaluate engagement metrics across all platforms to assess the effectiveness of content types and campaigns to help inform future strategies Proficient in photography and videography to create content that reflects authentic storytelling Help to monitor social media communication traffic and responding to timely requests and inquiries Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission , especially during peak activity times for campus events Position Skills and Abilities: Proficient and knowledgeable in all areas of social media strategies, development, and implementation - especially in a higher education setting Identify key contributors and working with a wide variety of constituents in building and maintaining that communication network Ability to establish and maintain short-term and long-term strategies Ability to monitor and assess social media analytics Proficient with digital devices to help with content creation Ability to communicate messages, ideas, and information effectively Superior judgement and interpersonal skills in working seamlessly and effectively with the campus community in partnership with vendors and campus departments Requirements: Bachelor's degree Required, Graduate degree Preferred 1+ years of social media experience and 2+ years in related fields is preferred Familiarity with a University environment is preferred Ability to work creatively and multi-task Proficient with related software such as Adobe Creative Suite, and other relevant social media management software to support content calendar planning, and engagement strategies Flexibility with schedule is important to attend some evening and weekend events To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Social Media Specialist position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#assistant-or-associate-dean-of-osteopathic-integration": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Dean of Osteopathic Integration",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Dean of Osteopathic Integration. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking an Assistant or Associate Dean of Osteopathic Integration for the John and Alice Butler College of Osteopathic Medicine. Position Summary: The Assistant or Associate Dean of Osteopathic Integration provides strategic leadership to ensure the osteopathic identity of the Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine program is explicit, coherent, and consistently experienced across the curriculum and clinical learning environment at John and Alice Butler College of Osteopathic Medicine (proposed, applicant seeking accreditation). This position leads the integration of Osteopathic Principles and Practice (OPP) and osteopathic philosophy throughout preclinical and clinical education; supports the quality and consistency of osteopathic manipulative medicine (OMM) instruction and assessment; and partners with faculty and clinical educators to reinforce person-centered, whole-person, and community-oriented care. The role supports accreditation readiness and continuous compliance with applicable standards (e.g., COCA) and contributes to student success and professional identity formation as developing osteopathic physicians. Primary Responsibilities: Lead the intentional integration of osteopathic philosophy, OPP, and clinical reasoning across the preclinical and clinical curriculum Collaborate with course and block leaders to embed osteopathic-relevant learning objectives, cases, and skills in foundational and clinical teaching Ensure horizontal and vertical integration of OMM/OPP content, including transitions from simulation/skills to clinical application Promote alignment of osteopathic integration with program competencies and outcomes (including COMLEX-related competencies, as appropriate) Oversee the quality, consistency, and continuous improvement of OMM/OPP instruction, including lab experiences and clinical correlation Establish and maintain assessment standards for osteopathic competencies (e.g., skills checklists, OSCE/clinical performance, professionalism and safety) Partner with assessment leadership to ensure valid, fair, and reliable evaluation processes, including remediation pathways for osteopathic skills Support faculty calibration to ensure consistent expectations and feedback across instructors and sites Develop and deliver faculty development that strengthens osteopathic integration, clinical teaching, feedback, and assessment Support clinical preceptors in reinforcing osteopathic principles during patient care and in evaluating osteopathic competencies Foster a culture of collaborative teaching excellence and continuous improvement centered on whole-person care Collaborate with Clinical Education leadership to promote osteopathic identity in clinical rotations and affiliated training sites Identify, develop, and support osteopathic-rich clinical learning experiences (including rural/community settings where appropriate) Partner on student preparation for clinical transitions (e.g., OMM application, documentation, communication, professionalism) Ensure osteopathic integration elements meet COCA expectations and are supported by clear documentation, curriculum maps, and outcomes evidence Participate in accreditation readiness activities, including narrative development, data review, and continuous compliance monitoring Contribute to academic policy development related to osteopathic competencies, OMM safety, professionalism, and progression Serve as a senior ambassador for the College's osteopathic identity in internal and external forums Collaborate with leaders across the COM and University to align osteopathic integration with institutional priorities Engage in scholarship, quality improvement, or educational innovation related to osteopathic education, as appropriate to rank and appointment Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate commitment to osteopathic philosophy and excellence in OMM/OPP teaching and clinical application Scholarly activity in osteopathic medical education, clinical practice innovation, or related quality improvement work Strong communication, collaboration, and change-management skills; ability to build alignment across disciplines and stakeholders Commitment to student-centered education, professionalism, and service to rural and underserved communities Experience developing competency-based assessment for psychomotor/clinical skills (e.g., OSCE design, rater calibration) Track record of faculty development, curriculum mapping, and integrated case-based or team-based learning Qualifications: Doctorate Degree Required Experience in medical education leadership (e.g., course/block leadership, OMM/OPP leadership, curriculum integration, faculty development) Prior experience directing or coordinating OMM/OPP programs, labs, or clinical skills curricula Working knowledge of accreditation expectations relevant to osteopathic education (e.g., COCA) and continuous quality improvement practices To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Assistant or Associate Dean of Osteopathic Integration for the John and Alice Butler College of Osteopathic Medicine position, please submit a cover letter, resume, three professional references, and UD employment application, located on our website, to HR@dbq.edu or to the Director of Human Resources, at the University of Dubuque, 2000 University Avenue, Dubuque, IA 52001. Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#chair-department-of-clinical-medicine": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Clinical Medicine",
      "description": "Chair, Department of Clinical Medicine. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Chair, Department of Clinical Medicine for the John and Alice Butler College of Osteopathic Medicine. Position Summary: The Chair of the Department of Clinical Medicine provides academic and administrative leadership for the clinical faculty and the delivery of the clinical skills curriculum throughout the four years of the Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine program. The Chair ensures that instruction in clinical reasoning, physical diagnosis, communication, and patient care is well integrated with biomedical and osteopathic principles and aligned with accreditation and competency standards. The position reports to the Associate Dean of Clinical Education and Graduate Medical Education and collaborates closely with the Associate Dean of Preclinical Education, the Director of Simulation and Clinical Skills, and course and clerkship directors. Primary Responsibilities: Lead the design, coordination, and continuous improvement of the clinical skills curriculum, including patient interviewing, physical examination, diagnostic reasoning, and documentation Ensure vertical integration of clinical skills content across preclinical and clinical years Oversee the development of assessment tools such as OSCEs, simulation exercises, and standardized patient encounters Collaborate with curriculum committees to align all clinical skills activities with COMLEX-USA competency domains and COCA standards Recruit, appoint, and evaluate clinical faculty and adjunct instructors across core and specialty disciplines Provide mentorship, peer review, and professional development opportunities to enhance instructional effectiveness and scholarly activity Foster an inclusive, collaborative department culture that values teamwork, professionalism, and innovation in clinical teaching Manage departmental operations, scheduling, and budget in coordination with the Associate Dean for Clinical Education & GME Collaborate with the Office of Simulation and Clinical Skills to ensure facilities, standardized patients, and resources meet educational goals Participate in strategic planning, policy development, and resource allocation for clinical education Monitor and evaluate clinical teaching quality through course reviews, student feedback, and performance outcomes Contribute to accreditation reporting, ensuring compliance with COCA and NBOME standards related to clinical instruction and assessment Support continuous quality improvement initiatives in alignment with institutional goals Maintain an active role in teaching and, where applicable, clinical practice Engage in scholarship in medical education, clinical pedagogy, or applied clinical science Represent the department and College on committees, at professional meetings, and in community partnerships Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Substantial teaching experience in medical education, preferably in clinical skills or clerkship coordination Strong communication, organizational, and mentoring skills Knowledge of COMLEX-USA competencies, COCA accreditation standards, and competency-based medical education Experience overseeing clinical faculty or directing clinical skills programs in an osteopathic or allopathic medical school Familiarity with simulation-based instruction and interprofessional education Qualifications: Medical degree (D.O. or M.D.) with board certification in a clinical specialty Demonstrate leadership and administrative experience in academic or clinical settings Record of scholarly productivity or innovation in medical education To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Chair, Department of Clinical Medicine for the John and Alice Butler College of Osteopathic Medicine position, please submit a cover letter, resume, three professional references, and UD employment application, located on our website, to HR@dbq.edu or to the Director of Human Resources, at the University of Dubuque, 2000 University Avenue, Dubuque, IA 52001. Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#full-time-faculty-in-computer-studies": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in Computer Studies",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in Computer Studies. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Full-time Faculty in Computer Studies . Position Summary: We are seeking an energetic, student-centered educator who will bring current technical knowledge, creative ideas, and a passion for mentoring students to a vibrant program spanning computer studies and information technology. The successful candidate will create engaging learning experiences, contribute to curriculum and program development, and help prepare students to lead and adapt in a rapidly changing digital landscape. The position includes opportunities to teach across a range of contemporary areas, including software engineering, data analytics, systems analysis and design, database systems, computer networks, and cloud infrastructure. Practical expertise in emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence, machine learning, or robotics is especially welcome. The ideal candidate will connect foundational knowledge with authentic problems, projects, and professional practice while working collaboratively with colleagues across disciplines. Primary Responsibilities: Mission Engage fully with the University's Mission through excellence in teaching and advising, ongoing scholarship and professional development, and active service to the campus and broader community Teaching and Advising Teach 24 credit hours per academic year in Computer Studies, Information Technology, and related areas as assigned Design learning experiences that actively engage students and accommodate a range of backgrounds, abilities, and learning needs Connect course content to contemporary technologies, authentic problems, and professional practice Assess student learning, provide clear and timely feedback, and use evidence to continually improve instruction Advise and mentor students in academic planning, career exploration, internships, research, and professional development. Maintain regular availability to support students outside of class Scholarship and Professional Development Maintain an active agenda of scholarship and professional growth appropriate to the discipline and the University's teaching-centered mission Remain current with emerging technologies, industry practices, and developments in teaching and learning Participate in relevant professional organizations, conferences, workshops, certifications, continuing education, or applied professional work Direct internships, tutorials, independent studies, and student research as needed Service Develop new courses and curricula and revise existing offerings to reflect changes in technology, professional practice, and student needs Contribute fresh ideas and collaborative leadership to the continued development of Computer Studies and Information Technology programs Build relationships with industry and community partners that support internships, projects, career pathways, and program relevance Support student recruitment, retention, and program outreach activities Participate in department and faculty meetings, convocations, commencements, shared governance, and University service Support in principle and practice the Mission of the University of Dubuque Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate expertise in one or more areas aligned with the program's teaching needs Evidence of effective teaching, training, mentoring, or the ability to create engaging undergraduate learning experiences Strong communication, collaboration, and organizational skills Ability to adapt to emerging technologies, changing professional expectations, and evolving educational practices Practice professional and collegial behavior, cultural competency, and inclusive approaches in all circumstances Qualifications: Master's degree is required; Doctorate degree is preferred A graduate degree in computer science, information systems, information technology, software engineering, data analytics, or a closely related field To learn more about what Dubuque, Iowa has to offer Click Here To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Full-time Faculty in the Computer Studies position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#full-time-faculty-in-the-physician-assistant-program": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in the Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in the Physician Assistant Program. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Full-time Faculty in the Physician Assistant Program for January 2027. Position Summary: This is a university faculty position with academic rank determined by the appointee's academic credentials and professional experience. The faculty member's primary responsibilities include developing and delivering evidence-based, face-to-face instruction in the basic medical and clinical sciences within their areas of expertise. Using a variety of instructional methods, the faculty member provides classroom lectures and clinical skills instruction, assists with laboratory teaching and demonstrations, evaluates student learning and performance, and advises students. Primary Responsibilities: Mission Engage fully with the University's mission through excellence in teaching and advising, ongoing scholarship and professional development, and active service to the campus and broader community Teaching and Advising Maintain a full-time credit load in collaboration with the department and the Office of the Vice President for Academic Affairs (VPAA) Participate in regular assessment and evaluation to foster continued pedagogical growth Deliver relevant and current curriculum using a variety of teaching methods and standardized tools that accurately reflect effectiveness of course content Be an active and present member of the campus community by supporting students outside of the classroom during regularly scheduled office hours Advise and mentor students and communicate early with any student in danger of failure or in need of individual counseling Scholarship and Professional Development Actively participate in academic and clinical scholarship, including but not limited to obtaining grant funding, research, article submissions, presentations, publications, peer review, and/or monitoring student research Build and maintain a professional portfolio for advancement in rank and tenure Maintain an active clinical practice with an average of 6 hours per week Undertake the necessary steps to stay certified or licensed in the discipline as expected by outside accreditation standards and/or best practices Service Participate in the ongoing assessment of the curricular and administrative aspects of the program through departmental meetings and committees Serve on and contribute to academic and/or University-wide committees Assist in program accreditation requirements and activities Represent the University in professional associations, conferences, or community partnerships related to the faculty member's field Other duties as assigned by the VPAA's office or department head in support of the University's Mission Provide service to the program, university, PA profession, and community, as assigned by the Program Director and/or Office of Academic Affairs Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate expertise in the academic discipline being taught through completed coursework or qualified experience Develop and use teaching methods that engage students and help them learn Communicate and collaborate clearly and effectively with students, staff, and faculty members Provide timely, constructive feedback on assignments and maintain an active gradebook Adapt to changes in the educational landscape, such as new technologies and educational standards Practice professional and collegial behavior, cultural competency, and inclusive approaches in all circumstances Qualifications: Graduate Degree in a healthcare-related area (PA-C, MD, DO) PAs must hold current NCCPA certification, a Master's Degree, and be eligible for licensure in the state of Iowa Minimum of two years of clinical experience is required Prior teaching in a PA program and prior precepting experience is preferred To learn more about what Dubuque, Iowa has to offer Click Here To apply to a growing, faith-based University for the Full-time Faculty in the Physician Assistant Program position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#full-time-faculty-in-nursing": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in Nursing",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in Nursing. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Full-time Faculty in Nursing . Position Summary: The University of Dubuque seeks a student-centered educator with experience in obstetrics, community health, and/or psychiatric nursing with a willingness to innovate and excel in teaching. The ideal candidate will foster a supportive learning environment while mentoring undergraduates in independent research and career preparation. The faculty member will be responsible for both clinical and classroom teaching and contributing to an already strong academic program. Primary Responsibilities: Mission Engage fully with the University's mission through excellence in teaching and advising, ongoing scholarship and professional development, and active service to the campus and broader community Teaching and Advising Maintain a full-time credit load of 24 credit hours per academic year, in collaboration with the department and the Office of the Vice President for Academic Affairs (VPAA) Participate in regular assessment and evaluation to foster continued pedagogical growth Respond to changes in student learning styles and technology by employing diverse teaching methods Be an active and present member of the campus community by supporting students outside of the classroom during regularly scheduled office hours Advise students on course selection, career pathways, and vocational goals as well as support student research, internships, and experiential learning opportunities Scholarship and Professional Development Maintain a scholarship agenda whether through publications, conference presentations, artistic exhibitions or performances, formal studies or continuing education Build and maintain a professional portfolio for advancement in rank and tenure Participate in campus professional development opportunities Maintain any required professional certifications or licensure in the appropriate discipline Service Participate in and contribute to all department meetings, faculty meetings, convocations, and commencements Serve on and contribute to academic and/or University-wide committees Assist in student recruitment and retention activities throughout the academic year Represent the University in professional associations, conferences, or community partnerships related to the faculty member's field Perform other duties as assigned by the VPAA's office or department head in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate expertise in the particular academic discipline being taught Develop and use teaching methods that engage students and support their learning Communicate clearly and effectively with students and provide timely feedback on assignments Adapt to changes in the educational landscape, including, but not limited to new technologies and educational standards Maintain professional and collegial behavior Strong organizational skills, including managing a flexible schedule, multiple projects and student needs Qualifications: MSN required; Doctoral degree preferred Experience in medical-surgical, obstetrics, community health, and/or psychiatric nursing To learn more about what Dubuque, Iowa has to offer Click Here To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Full-time Faculty in Nursing position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#full-time-faculty-in-mathematics": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in Mathematics",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in Mathematics. The University of Dubuque is a growing, faith-based University that is seeking a Full-time Faculty in Mathematics for Fall 2027. Position Summary: This is a unique opportunity for a full-time Mathematics faculty member to contribute to a vibrant and growing program that serves students across a wide range of academic disciplines. The successful candidate will play a central role in teaching undergraduate mathematics courses, including calculus, statistics, quantitative reasoning, and other foundational mathematics courses - while helping to shape curriculum, support student success, and advance innovative approaches to mathematics education. We are seeking an educator who brings energy, creativity, and a passion for mentoring students, and who is excited to create engaging learning experiences that demonstrate the relevance and beauty of mathematics across disciplines and in the world around us. We are especially interested in candidates who are enthusiastic collaborators who bring fresh ideas, a student-centered mindset, and a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring. Primary Responsibilities: Mission Engage fully with the University's mission through excellence in teaching and advising, ongoing scholarship and professional development, and active service to the campus and broader community Teaching and Advising Maintain a full-time credit load of 24 credit hours per academic year, in collaboration with the department and the Office of the Vice President for Academic Affairs (VPAA) Participate in regular assessment and evaluation to foster continued pedagogical growth Design and deliver engaging, student-centered learning experiences that inspire curiosity, quantitative reasoning, and mathematical confidence. Leverage innovative and evidence-based teaching practices to support diverse learners and evolving educational technologies Foster problem solving, critical thinking, and analytical reasoning while helping students apply mathematical concepts to real-world contexts and across disciplines Support students outside the classroom through regularly scheduled office hours and mentor students through academic advising, undergraduate research, internships where appropriate, and other experiential learning opportunities Scholarship and Professional Development Pursue an active scholarly or creative agenda appropriate to the discipline and share outcomes through publications, presentations, or other scholarly activities Build and maintain a professional portfolio for advancement in rank and tenure Participate in campus professional development opportunities Maintain awareness of evolving disciplinary standards, pedagogical best practices, and emerging technologies in mathematics education Service Serve as a key contributor in developing and strengthening the mathematics curriculum, student success initiatives, and interdisciplinary collaborations Participate in and contribute to all department meetings, faculty meetings, convocations, and commencements Serve on and contribute to academic and/or University-wide committees Assist in student recruitment and retention activities throughout the academic year Represent the University through professional organizations, conferences, outreach activities, or community partnerships related to mathematics and mathematics education Perform other duties as assigned by the VPAA's office or department head in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate a passion for teaching, mentoring, and contributing to a collaborative and innovative academic environment Exhibit expertise in mathematics through completed coursework or qualified experience Design and apply instructional strategies that actively engage students and promote deep conceptual understanding Teach students effectively with a wide range of mathematical preparation and learning backgrounds Communicate and collaborate clearly and effectively with students, staff, and faculty members Provide timely, constructive feedback on assignments and maintain an active gradebook Integrate appropriate instructional technologies and adapt to changes in educational practices and standards Practice professional and collegial behavior, cultural competency, and inclusive approaches in all circumstances Qualifications: Graduate degree in Mathematics or a closely related field required; Doctoral degree preferred Emphasis in statistics or applied mathematics preferred To learn more about what Dubuque, Iowa has to offer Click Here To apply with a growing, faith-based University for the Full-time Faculty in Mathematics position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#full-time-faculty-in-engineering": {
      "title": "Full-time Faculty in Engineering",
      "description": "Full-time Faculty in Engineering. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Full-time Faculty in Engineering . Position Summary: This is a unique opportunity for a founding full-time Engineering faculty member to help build and shape a growing program from the ground up. The successful candidate will play a central role in designing and delivering core undergraduate courses - such as design, physics, statics, dynamics, electronics, materials, and thermodynamics - while driving innovation in curriculum, labs, and student experiences. We are seeking an educator who brings energy, creativity, and a passion for mentoring students, and who is excited to develop a forward-looking program aligned with modern engineering practice and industry needs. We are especially interested in candidates who are enthusiastic builders - educators who bring fresh ideas, a collaborative spirit, and a desire to create meaningful, hands-on learning experiences for students. Primary Responsibilities: Mission Engage fully with the University's mission through excellence in teaching and advising, ongoing scholarship and professional development, and active service to the campus and broader community Teaching and Advising Maintain a full-time credit load of 24 credit hours per academic year, in collaboration with the department and the Office of the Vice President for Academic Affairs (VPAA) Participate in regular assessment and evaluation to foster continued pedagogical growth Design and deliver engaging, student-centered learning experiences that inspire curiosity and deepen understanding. Leverage innovative and evidence-based teaching practices to support diverse learners and evolving educational technologies Advance entrepreneurial-minded learning by inspiring students to think creatively, take initiative, and apply engineering solutions to real-world challenges Be an active and present member of the campus community by supporting students outside of the classroom during regularly scheduled office hours and mentor and support students as developing engineers through advising, research opportunities, internships, and experiential learning Scholarship and Professional Development Pursue an active scholarly or creative agenda appropriate to the discipline and share outcomes through publications, presentations, exhibitions, or performances Build and maintain a professional portfolio for advancement in rank and tenure Participate in campus professional development opportunities Maintain awareness of evolving disciplinary standards and best practices through ongoing professional development and engagement with the broader engineering community Service Serve as a key contributor in developing and shaping the program's curriculum, courses, laboratories, and facilities as part of its ongoing growth and success Participate in and contribute to all department meetings, faculty meetings, convocations, and commencements Serve on and contribute to academic and/or University-wide committees Assist in student recruitment and retention activities throughout the academic year Represent the University in professional associations, conferences, or community partnerships related to the faculty member's field Perform other duties as assigned by the VPAA's office or department head in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate a passion for teaching, mentoring, and contributing to a collaborative and innovative academic environment Exhibit expertise in the particular academic discipline being taught through completed coursework or qualified experience Design and apply instructional strategies that actively engage students and support their learning Communicate and collaborate clearly and effectively with students, staff, and faculty members Provide timely, constructive feedback on assignments and maintain an active gradebook Adapt to changes in the educational landscape, such as new technologies and educational standards Practice professional and collegial behavior, cultural competency, and inclusive approaches in all circumstances Qualifications: Graduate degree Required; Doctoral degree Preferred Review of applicants will begin October 1, 2026. To learn more about what Dubuque, Iowa has to offer Click Here To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Full-time Faculty in Engineering position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmative Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#full-time-faculty-in-aviation": {
      "title": "Full-Time Faculty in Aviation",
      "description": "Full-Time Faculty in Aviation. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Full-time Faculty in Aviation . Position Summary: This position offers a unique opportunity to influence the aviation industry by mentoring the next generation of aviation professionals. Your expertise in aviation could be the driving force that propels our students to new heights. Primary Responsibilities: Mission Support in principle and practice the Mission of the University Teaching and Advising Teach 24 credit hours per academic year as assigned by the Department or by the VPAAs office Employ diverse teaching methods to accommodate varying student learning styles Develop new courses or curricula or revise existing ones when appropriate Regularly evaluate teaching methods and use data to continually improve instructional strategies Direct internships, tutorials, independent studies, student research as needed Serve as an academic advisor and mentor to students, providing guidance on course selection and career goals Maintain regular office hours to support students outside of class Scholarship and Professional Development Maintain a scholarship agenda whether through publications, conference presentations, artistic exhibitions or performances, formal studies or continuing education. Attend campus workshops related to the specific teaching field or to learning in general Maintain any required professional certifications or licensure in the appropriate discipline Service Active participation in or contribution to the work of the University as well as to that of the broader academic community Attend all department meetings, faculty meetings, convocations, and commencements. Serve on academic and/or University-wide committees Assist in student recruitment activities Participate in professional organizations related to the faculty member's discipline Other duties as assigned by the VPAA's office or department head in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate expertise in the particular academic discipline being taught Develop and use teaching methods that engage students and help them learn Communicate clearly and effectively with students and provide timely feedback on assignments Adapt to changes in the educational landscape, such as new technologies and educational standards Maintain professional and collegial behavior Cultural competency and diversity-oriented approach Qualifications: Graduate Degree Required; Doctorate Degree Preferred FAA ground or flight instructor certification capable of instructing private, instrument, and commercial ground school courses; multi-engine preferred Experience with turbine/jet operations is highly desired, especially if coupled with FAA part 121 or 135 experience To learn more about what Dubuque, Iowa has to offer Click Here . To apply with a growing faith based University for the Full-time Faculty in Aviation position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#adjunct-faculty": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty. The University of Dubuque is a diverse, Christian, and forward-thinking educational community with a rich history of over 150 years of academic excellence. Established in 1852, we are committed to preparing our students for success by helping them discover their passion and purpose. Whether on campus or part of our UDOnline community, you will be part of a globally diverse group of learners committed to lifelong learning and service. Why Choose the University of Dubuque Online: Academic Excellence: Leverage our 150+ years of educational experience. Inclusive Community: Thrive in a culture that fosters diversity and responsible self-expression. lobal Perspective: Engage with a globally diverse community. Flexibility: Enjoy the convenience of online learning without sacrificing quality. UDOnline MBA Program is currently accepting applications for adjunct faculty within the following specializations: Business Analytics Finance Marketing Leadership Responsibilities: Develop and deliver course content in a virtual setting Engage students in active learning Assess student performance and provide timely feedback Qualifications: A completed doctoral degree (Ph.D., DBA, or DM) in Business, Management, Marketing, or a related field. A master's degree with significant industry experience may also be considered. Prior teaching experience, particularly in an online environment, is highly desired. How to Apply: Interested candidates should submit a cover letter, CV, and contact information for three professional references and UD employment application, located on our website, to HR@dbq.edu or the Director of Human Resources, at the University of Dubuque, 2000 University Avenue, Dubuque, IA 52001. Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#adjunct-instructors-in-nursing": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructors in Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructors in Nursing. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking Adjunct Instructors in Nursing . Position Summary: The Adjunct Nursing Faculty member provides face-to-face instruction and clinical supervision for students in medical-surgical or psychiatric–mental health settings, depending on qualifications. This role includes evaluating student performance, ensuring safe clinical practice, and using program-approved educational platforms to assess learning. The faculty member supports student growth through timely feedback, contributes to an inclusive learning environment, and participates in required training and meetings while upholding the mission and values of the University. Primary Responsibilities: Serve as clinical instructor in medical-surgical or psychiatric-mental health clinical settings Instruct face-to-face in medical-surgical or psychiatric-mental health courses, depending on applicant qualifications Assess student learning through written assessments, case studies, assignments, and exams utilizing program specified educational platforms Supervise, instruct, and evaluate students in clinical settings to ensure safe and effective practice Offer constructive, timely feedback to support student learning and professional growth Participate in required orientations, training, and adjunct faculty meetings Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Adapt to changes in the educational landscape, such as new technologies and educational standards Ability to foster a positive, respectful, and inclusive learning environment Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with a passion for medical education Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with faculty, staff, and clinical partners Maintain professional and collegial behavior Minimum Qualifications: BSN required; MSN preferred Current unencumbered Iowa Nursing license Experience teaching, precepting, or mentoring students in a clinical or academic setting Knowledge of, and commitment to, the university's philosophy, mission and core values This position is part of an ongoing talent pool. Qualified candidates may be contacted when openings become available. To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Adjunct Instructors in Nursing , please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#adjunct-instructors-in-flight-operations-or-aviation-management": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructors in Flight Operations or Aviation Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructors in Flight Operations or Aviation Management. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking Adjunct Instructors in Flight Operations or Aviation Management for Fall 2026. Primary Responsibilities: Teach aviation courses, including flight operations, aviation management, and UAS Teach pertinent course content using lectures, demonstrations, class discussions, and other appropriate modes of educational delivery that promote educational and learning processes Prepare course outlines and syllabi, develop course and lesson plans, and engage in the selection of textbooks and other teaching aids necessary for the instruction of courses as requested Assess learners' submissions in a timely manner and provide feedback Submit course-related reports and assessments as requested by the University or Department of Aviation Maintain course standards set by the department Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate expertise in the academic discipline being taught Develop and use teaching methods that engage students and help them learn Communicate clearly and effectively with students and provide timely feedback on assignments Adapt to changes in the educational landscape, such as new technologies and educational standards Maintain professional and collegial behavior Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in aviation or a related field and a minimum of 3 years of professional aviation experience Ability to utilize and integrate technology into content delivery and assessment techniques Ability to communicate and work with a diverse population of students both in and outside the classroom Excellent written and oral communication skills Prior teaching experience or evidence of teaching potential and/or corporate/industry training Knowledge of, and commitment to, the university's philosophy, mission, and core values Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate degree in aviation, aviation education, or a closely related field FAA ground or flight instructor certification capable of instructing private, instrument, commercial, multi-engine, and flight instructor ground school courses Experience with turbine/jet operations is highly desired, especially if coupled with FAA part 121 or 135 experience To apply with a growing faith based University for the Adjunct Instructor position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to HR@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#online-adjunct-faculty": {
      "title": "Online Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Online Adjunct Faculty. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking Online Adjunct Faculty for Fall 2026. Position Summary: The University of Dubuque is a diverse, Christian, and forward-thinking educational community with a rich history of over 150 years of academic excellence. Established in 1852, we are committed to preparing our students for success by helping them discover their passion and purpose. You will be part of a globally diverse group of learners committed to lifelong learning and service. Primary Responsibilities: Develop and deliver course content in a virtual setting Engage students in active learning Assess learner's submissions in a timely manner and provide feedback to learners Submit course-related reports as requested by the University Maintain course standards set by the department Maintain communication with the coordinator of this position Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Academic Departments: Business Criminal Justice Cybersecurity Psychology Liberal Studies B.A. (Healthcare Administrations, Management & Leadership) Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrated mastery of subject matter Adapt to changes in the educational landscape, such as new technologies and educational standards Maintain professional and collegial behavior Minimum Qualifications: Minimum of a Master's degree with 18 graduate hours in the discipline Ability to utilize and integrate technology into content delivery and assessment techniques Ability to communicate and work with a diverse population of students Prior teaching experience or must demonstrate evidence of teaching potential and/or corporate/industry training Knowledge of, and commitment to, the university's philosophy, mission, and core values To apply with a growing faith based University for the Online Adjunct Faculty position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to HR@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#graduate-assistant-in-the-heritage-center-audience-services": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant in the Heritage Center (Audience Services)",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant in the Heritage Center (Audience Services). The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Graduate Assistant in the Heritage Center (Audience Services) for the 2026-2027 term, with a potential renewal for 2027-2028. Primary Responsibilities: Collaborative with Heritage Center staff, UD's Fine and Performing Arts Department, University Relations, Advancement, and Alumni offices to advance the performing arts on campus Report to the Director of Audience Services for box office and FOH (Front of House) operations and to the Executive Director on event/facility marketing and programming issues Maintain strong public relations and deliver high-quality customer service to all Heritage Center patrons and users, both on and off campus Coordinate and maintain the volunteer ushering program and class-credit ushering program for Heritage Center Supervise all FOH (Front of House) staff, including (and not limited to) ticketing assistants and ushers Oversee venue seating layouts for each event and assist to ensure that all FOH (Front of House) responsibilities are executed efficiently and with a customer-focused approach Be available to support pre- and post-show functions held in conjunction with theater events Compile and share post-event reports with management as requested Serve as a liaison for on-site catering services and collaborate with Heritage Center staff to support FOH (Front of House) needs and lobby displays Perform other duties in support of the University's Mission Requirements: Bachelor's degree is required and the position is conditional based on acceptance into University of Dubuque Masters' program Allow flexibility in scheduling, as evening and weekend hours are often required. Work hours will vary based on the Heritage Center event schedule Knowledge of the VBO ticketing system for software maintenance, trouble shooting, and updates Utilize excellent communication skills - verbal, written, and interpersonal High level of organization and attention to detail All graduate tuition is waived for the student for the term in which they serve as a GA. In return for a waiver of tuition, the assistantship recipient agrees to provide service to the University equivalent to twenty (20) hours per week. This position is eligible for a stipend. For more information, click here . To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Graduate Assistant in the Heritage Center (Audience Services) position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to HR@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#graduate-assistant-for-women-s-soccer": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant for Women's Soccer",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant for Women's Soccer. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Graduate Assistant for Women's Soccer for the 2026-2027 term, with a potential renewal for 2027-2028. The University of Dubuque is an NCAA Division III institution and a member of the American Rivers Conference. Primary Responsibilities: Analyze performance and instruct athletes in techniques and strategies in preparation for and during athletic competitions Assist the head coach in the coordination of administrative areas of program management including, but not limited to, scheduling of competitions and practices, travel plans, and equipment Assist program with all phases of competitive NCAA and ARC compliant recruiting Assist with monitoring academic progress of all student-athletes on the team, in connection with the coaching staff, compliance coordinator and athletic director Execute practice and game planning/evaluation, including video coordination and breakdown Manage equipment usage Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Requirements: Bachelor's degree is required and the position is conditional based on acceptance into University of Dubuque Masters' program Valid driver's license Flexibility with schedule (ex. evening or weekend commitments) High level of organization and attention to detail Proficiency in Microsoft Office Prior coaching experience or playing experience (goal keeping experience preferred) Effective communication skills; both orally and written All graduate tuition is waived for the student for the term in which they serve as a GA. In return for a waiver of tuition, the assistantship recipient agrees to provide service to the University equivalent to twenty (20) hours per week. This position is eligible for a stipend. For more information, click here . To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Graduate Assistant for Women's Soccer position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to HR@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#graduate-assistant-in-the-wendt-center-for-character-and-leadership": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant in the Wendt Center for Character and Leadership",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant in the Wendt Center for Character and Leadership. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Graduate Assistant in the Wendt Center for Character and Leadership for the 2026-2027 term, with a potential renewal for 2027-2028. Primary Responsibilities: Plan, organize, and lead one character focused co-curricular event per week, engaging both Wendt Scholars and all UD students Assist with the setup, facilitation, and logistics of additional Wendt Center events as needed Actively promote character education events, encouraging broad participation across campus Partner with Wendt Ambassadors and Scholars, student organizations, campus groups, faculty, and staff to develop engaging, mission-driven programming that fosters character development and community connection Maintain records of attendance, feedback, and event effectiveness to inform future programming Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Requirements: Bachelor's degree is required and the position is conditional based on acceptance into University of Dubuque Masters' program Strong organizational and leadership skills Experience or interest in event planning, student development, and character education Ability to work collaboratively and independently in a dynamic campus environment Excellent communication and interpersonal skills All graduate tuition is waived for the student for the term in which they serve as a GA. In return for a waiver of tuition, the assistantship recipient agrees to provide service to the University equivalent to twenty (20) hours per week. For more information, click here . To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Graduate Assistant in the Wendt Center for Character and Leadership position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to HR@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#graduate-assistant-for-track-and-field": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant for Track and Field",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant for Track and Field. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a Graduate Assistant for Track and Field with an emphasis on jumps or throws for the 2026-2027 term, with a potential renewal for 2027-2028. The University of Dubuque is a NCAA Division III institution and a member of the American Rivers Conference. Primary Responsibilities: Instruct athletes in jumping or throwing techniques and strategies, etc. Recruitment of prospective student-athletes Coordination of team operations such as travel, camps, and home meets Monitor eligibility status and promotion of academic progress for student-athletes Manage team equipment and apparel Participate and assist with camps, clinics, exhibitions, and campus activities Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Requirements: Bachelor's degree is required and the position is conditional based on acceptance into University of Dubuque Masters' program High level of organization and attention to detail Proficiency in Microsoft Office Preferred Qualifications: Prior coaching experience and/or prior experience as an athlete Effective communication skills; both orally and written Proficiency in social media All graduate tuition is waived for the student for the term in which they serve as a GA. In return for a waiver of tuition, the assistantship recipient agrees to provide service to the University equivalent to twenty (20) hours per week. This position is eligible for a stipend. For more information, click here . To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Graduate Assistant for Track and Field position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to HR@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#adjunct-instructors-in-the-division-of-natural-sciences": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructors in the Division of Natural Sciences",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructors in the Division of Natural Sciences. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking Adjunct Instructors in the Division of Natural Sciences for Spring 2027. Position Summary: Anatomy and Physiology Teach the lecture and laboratory components of an Anatomy and Physiology II course during the Spring 2027 semester. This is the second semester of a two-part course sequence. Materials and guidance regarding the content to be covered in this second-semester course can be provided. The course includes three 50-minute lecture sessions per week and two cadaver-based laboratory sections, each meeting for three hours. Teach, lecture, and lab for a Cell biology course during the Spring 2027 semester. This will include the lecture that meets three times a week for 50 min and two lab sections that are 3 hours each. Cell Biology Teach, lecture, and lab for a Cell biology course during the Spring 2027 semester. This will include the lecture that meets three times a week for 50 min and two lab sections that are 3 hours each. Primary Responsibilities: Teach relevant course content through lectures, demonstrations, class discussions, and other appropriate instructional methods that support effective teaching and learning Prepare course outlines and syllabi, develop course and lesson plans, and select textbooks and other instructional materials as requested Evaluate learner submissions in a timely manner, provide constructive feedback, and submit course-related reports as requested by the University Maintain departmental course standards and communicate regularly with the position coordinator Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Position Skills and Abilities: Demonstrate mastery of subject matter of cell biology or anatomy and physiology Adapt to changes in the educational landscape, such as new technologies and educational standards Maintain professional and collegial behavior Excellent written and oral communication skills Knowledge of, and commitment to, the university's philosophy, mission, and core values Requirements: Minimum of a master's degree in biology or a related field. Ability to utilize and integrate technology into content delivery and assessment techniques Ability to communicate and work with a diverse population of students both in and outside the classroom Prior teaching experience or must demonstrate evidence of teaching potential and/or corporate/industry training To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Adjunct Instructors in the Division of Natural Sciences position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#part-time-adjunct-faculty-for-the-life-program": {
      "title": "Part-time Adjunct Faculty for the LIFE Program",
      "description": "Part-time Adjunct Faculty for the LIFE Program. The University of Dubuque (UD) is seeking Part-time LIFE Adjunct Faculty in multiple academic areas to teach in its accelerated adult program. UD is a diverse, Christian, and forward-thinking educational community. Through its Learning Institute for Fulfillment and Engagement (LIFE), the university offers accelerated, face-to-face undergraduate and graduate programs targeted to adult learners. Each course generally meets one night per week (Monday through Thursday) for five weeks. Responsibilities: Instruct face-to-face, accelerated course for 3 credit hours (Biology course and some accounting courses are 4 credits) Deliver established curriculum effectively for a five-week course. Utilize established syllabus, learning objectives, and assignments to customize provided LMS course template so students may access course details two weeks prior to first class Provide timely, specific, substantive feedback to students in and outside of class times Academic Departments: Accounting Biology Business Criminal Justice English Composition & Literature Finance Health Care Administration Math (College Algebra, Statistics) Qualifications: Master's or PhD degree in the relevant discipline Five or more years of experience working in the field preferred University teaching experience preferred Commitment to the mission of the University and to its approach to adult, accelerated education To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Part-time LIFE Adjunct Faculty position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    },
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#temporary-track-and-field-coach": {
      "title": "Temporary Track and Field Coach",
      "description": "Temporary Track and Field Coach. The University of Dubuque is a growing faith-based University that is seeking a part-time Temporary Track and Field Coach . Position Summary: Reporting to the Head Coach, this Temporary Coach assists in coaching student athletes for the Track & Field team that is consistent with the University Mission and strategic plan, as well as the Student Success Commitment. Additionally, this position assists in meeting all compliance and eligibility requirements for the University, the American Rivers Conference, and the NCAA; and promoting the safety and well-being of all student-athletes. Primary Responsibilities: Assist in practice planning, execution and instruction Assist in the collaboration with campus partners and athletic administration regarding facility use, upkeep, and resource management Effectively live and model the UD Mission and engage the campus and surrounding communities in a manner that allows for the retention and persistence of UD students Collaborate with and serve the campus community Facilitate educational opportunities and compliance to all University, ARC, and NCAA rules and regulations Serve as a collaborative and valued team member within the athletic department Serve as a Title IX Campus Security Authority Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Coach Willingness and ability to be an active participant in following applicable safety rules and regulations, including necessary training and drills Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's Mission Skills and Abilities: Strong active listening and effective communication skills Strong social emotional skills and a student-centered approach to teaching and learning Clear capacity for effective conflict resolution and mediation High ethical standards Cultural competency and diversity-oriented approach Strong technological skill set Ability to effectively work in a team environment Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Previous coaching experience preferred Demonstrated commitment to addressing issues of diversity, inclusion, hospitality, and equity for a diverse student population and campus stakeholders Appreciation for and ability to work within a collaborative campus community and the ability to assist in building collaborative alliances to serve students and the campus communities To apply with a growing faith-based University for the Temporary Track and Field Coach position, please submit a UD Employment Application with an attached cover letter, resume, and three professional references or email application materials to hr@dbq.edu . Affirmation Action/Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. For more information regarding the Jeanne Clery Act, please go to https://www.dbq.edu/SafetySecurity/JeanneCleryAct/"
    }
  },
  "rows": {
    "https://www.dbq.edu/AboutUD/Employment/Jobs/#director-of-career-success-and-community-engagement": {
